Subject: [PATCH sched_ext/for-7.5 0/7] selftests/sched_ext: Fix scheduler leaks on early return
To: Tejun Heo <tj@kernel.org>
Cc: David Vernet <void@manifault.com>,
    Andrea Righi <arighi@nvidia.com>,
    Changwoo Min <changwoo@igalia.com>,
    Tao Cui <cuitao@kylinos.cn>,
    Ching-Chun Huang <jserv@ccns.ncku.edu.tw>,
    Chia-Ping Tsai <chia7712@gmail.com>,
    sched-ext@lists.linux.dev,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

Many sched_ext selftests destroy their struct_ops link at the end of
run(), after SCX_*() checks that return early on failure. A failing
check then leaves the BPF scheduler loaded, and the tests that run
after it fail to attach until something unloads it. If one of them is
peek_dsq, its cleanup() crashes the runner and the rest of the run is
lost.

Andrea suggested applying the fix from commit e18002d2c791
("selftests/sched_ext: Fix select_cpu_dfl link leak on early return")
to the other selftests [1]. This series does that:

  1: add scx_test.h helpers that keep the skeleton and the link in the
     test context, so cleanup() always tears them down
  2: convert the tests that attach once in run() to those helpers, and
     reap every child in the fork-based ones before reporting
  3: fix the tests that open the skeleton outside setup() or attach
     more than once, and route their early returns through the teardown
  4: fix the peek_dsq runner crash and its own link leak
  5: fix the same leak in enable_cmask
  6: fix the leaks that the new SCX_ASSERT_ALIVE() and EXIT_KIND()
     early returns added to create_dsq, maximal and prog_run
  7: make the runner fail and name a test that leaves a scheduler
     loaded, so a future leak points at the right test

The series is on top of Tao's selftest fixes in for-7.4 and keeps
their bounded exit waits and SCX_ASSERT_ALIVE() checks. Those make
more checks fail cleanly, which is why patch 6 is needed.

Tested with vng on for-7.5: all tests pass, with enq_blocked and
nohz_tick skipped as they need CONFIG_SCHED_PROXY_EXEC and nohz_full=.
Forcing failures in create_dsq, maximal, init_enable_count, exit,
hotplug, prog_run and enq_select_cpu now fails only those seven tests.
Without the series, forcing the create_dsq failure makes the tests
after it fail to attach, and the runner then crashes in peek_dsq.

checkpatch --strict reports 1 warning and 6 checks on patch 1, all
about the new token-pasting macros in scx_test.h.

[1] https://lore.kernel.org/r/af2aD8-tFi_yhPOV@gpd4

